<p>The Trump administration is considering temporarily lifting sanctions on Iranian oil already at sea as it tries to steady energy markets rattled by the war in the Middle East. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the move could make about 140 million barrels available and help lower global oil prices after the conflict disrupted supplies and Iranian attacks crippled the Strait of Hormuz, a route that carries roughly 20% of the world’s oil supply. Bessent said the administration has several ways to limit price spikes, including further releases from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve after already making 172 million barrels available. A person familiar with White House planning told Politico that officials have discussed adding as much as 100 million more barrels, though some military advisers favor a smaller release of around 50 million because they worry about draining reserves while regional energy infrastructure remains under threat.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/LEXntC-DfEtu2auN0-ES88KWuWhSpdBbwHBVaipvjZ3Wbx180yr4PrXsCEzwwu2gDbNnIWUvs1-yDuWbn80h9YyNCTRMkiQJ2OcE-N6oBbFuz2kHkGni6E3M7Xgj0-qYImJFQ2TRwFEulDLEVLamp8CHEw5-0qZ5kcZnltuqWcNmBhMIOrV2Evl8XjzF2BlmSmHIO8_KuZ4' alt='Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the sanctions exemption would apply to about 140 million barrels of Iranian oil that were currently at sea.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Consumer pressure: Al-Monitor reported that the policy review reflects a push to ease high energy costs now reaching U.S. consumers even as Washington continues its campaign against Tehran.</li><li>Policy limit: A Trump administration official told Al-Monitor that oil and gas export restrictions are not under consideration, signaling that the debate is focused on supply relief rather than limiting outbound energy trade.</li><li>Campaign context: Politico said the administration has weighed market-stabilizing options since the United States and Israel launched a joint operation in February.</li><li>Qatar shock: NDTV reported that prices surged again after Iran struck Qatar’s largest liquefied natural gas facility and threatened broader attacks on regional energy infrastructure.</li></ul><blockquote>In essence, we will be using the Iranian barrels against the Iranians to keep the price down for the next 10 or 14 days, as we continue this campaign - Scott Bessent</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Scott Bessent: The Treasury secretary presented sanction relief for oil already afloat as a short-term way to cap prices while military operations continue, and said Washington still has other levers it can pull. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/19/iranian-oil-sanctions-middle-east-war-00835804'>Politico</a>)</li><li>White House planners: Officials have discussed releasing up to 100 million more barrels from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve, though the administration is still debating how far to go. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/19/iranian-oil-sanctions-middle-east-war-00835804'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Military advisers: Some advisers are pushing for a smaller reserve draw of about 50 million barrels because they worry that a deeper release would leave the United States with less cushion if more Middle East oil and gas infrastructure is damaged. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/19/iranian-oil-sanctions-middle-east-war-00835804'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Trump administration official: One administration official said Washington is considering easing pressure on Iranian crude already at sea, but not broader restrictions on oil and gas exports. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/us-mulls-lifting-sanctions-iranian-oil-sea-despite-war-tehran'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/19/iranian-oil-sanctions-middle-east-war-00835804'>Trump administration may unsanction some Iranian oil as energy prices spike, Bessent says</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/19/us/politics/iran-oil-sanctions.html'>U.S. Encourages Flow of Iranian Oil While It Battles Iran</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-may-remove-sanctions-on-iranian-oil-stranded-in-tankers-bessent-says'>US may remove sanctions on Iranian oil stranded in tankers, says Bessent</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-may-unsanction-iran-oil-already-being-shipped-treasury-chief-11240046#publisher=newsstand'>US May &#x27;Unsanction&#x27; Iran Oil Already Being Shipped: Treasury Chief</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/us-mulls-lifting-sanctions-iranian-oil-sea-despite-war-tehran'>US mulls lifting sanctions on Iranian oil at sea despite war on Tehran</a> - al-monitor.com</li></ul>